  "conclusion": "OrthoHMM high_sensitivity outperforms the pre-phylogenetic OrthoFinder 3.1.5 MCL checkpoint on both primary benchmarks: +11.7 OrthoBench F-score points and +0.137589 QfO mean. Full OrthoFinder remains better than both. The pre-phylogenetic checkpoint has high OrthoBench recall but severe over-grouping; OrthoFinder's tree and reconciliation stages recover 20.4 precision points at a cost of only 1.1 recall points and improve the QfO mean by 0.237111."
